  "resolution": {
    "eligibility": "A broken unit of the catalog in its Location in the RPh, once per Player Turn and with no other RPh action (A3.1, A10.6); rallied by an unbroken friendly leader in the same Location (A10.6, A10.7), or by Self-Rally when no Good Order friendly leader is there (A10.63): a broken leader (A10.71), a unit with Self-Rally capability, or the first MMC Rally attempt of the side's own RPh (A18.11); never by a Disrupted unit (A19.12).",
    "drm": "+4 under DM (A10.62); the rallying leader's modifier, one worse when he is wounded (A10.7, A10.72, A17.3), or +1 for Self-Rally (A10.63); -1 in woods or a building (A10.61).",
    "morale": "The broken Morale Level (A10.4), one lower when the unit is wounded (A17.3).",
    "result": "Rallied on a Final DR at most the Morale Level (A10.6); an Original 12 is Fate: Casualty Reduction and no rally (A10.64, A7.302), a leader's wound taking a Wound Severity dr (A17.11); an Original 2 on the A18.11 Self-Rally rallies the unit (A18.11).",
    "deviations": "None: an Original 2 on a leader rally calls for a Heat of Battle DR, and one on the A18.11 Self-Rally for a Leader Creation dr (A18.2: -1 German, +1 Russian, -1 for a Morale Level of 8 or more, +1 for 6 or less, +1 broken; 6 or less creates a 6+1 to an 8-1 of the unit's nationality). Every Heat of Battle result is taken (R30.2, R30.7).",
    "concealment": "The unit and a concealed rallying leader lose \"?\" in the LOS of a Good Order enemy within 16 hexes (A12.141); a Reduced or wounded unit loses it regardless (A12.14).",
    "heatOfBattle": "An Original MC DR of 2 on a MC or a leader's rally calls for a Heat of Battle DR with -1 elite, -1 NKVD, +1 broken (before the MC or by it), +1 Inexperienced, and the nationality DRM (A15.1, A25.25): a Final DR of 6 or less creates a hero of the unit's nationality, or makes a leader heroic, rallying him (A15.21); 5 to 8 Battle Hardens the unit (A15.3, A10.8, A25.25; ruling R28.7); 9 to 11, or 12 or more for a Fanatic unit, makes it berserk, rallied, unpinned, and without \"?\", unless no Known enemy unit is in its LOS, when it is Battle Hardened instead (A15.4, A15.42, A15.44); 12 or more breaks and Disrupts it, and it surrenders to one of its ADJACENT captors, if any (A15.5). A leader who goes berserk takes the other friendly units of his Location with him on a passed NTC with his leadership DRM (A15.41). A berserk or Battle Hardened unit rallies though the Rally DR failed; a surrendering unit is broken again."
  },
